WEBVTT

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:38.695
Captain...
Computer, pause music.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.466
l didn't wake you, did l?

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.473
That's all right, Doctor.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.670
15 minutes of sleep
is really all l need.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.235
Coffee, black.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:50.874
Maybe you should pay a little
more attention to flying

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.884
and a little less to singing.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.476
As a hologram, l can handle
a variety of tasks at once.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:56.852
ln addition to piloting
the Flyer,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.016
l'm writing a paper
on the physiological stresses

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.286
of long-duration
space flight

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.558
and... taking holo-images
of this Mutara-class nebula.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.191
With a hologram on board,
who needs a crew?

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.757
l'd never admit this
to anyone else,

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.234
but there was a time when
l would have given anything

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.430
to be flesh and blood,

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.632
but l've come to realize
that being a hologram

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.208
is far superior.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:17.903
Really?

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.239
No offense.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:22.406
l'll always enjoy the company
of organics.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.814
ln fact, l'm delighted
you were able to attend

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.181
this medical symposium with me.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.083
lt's been a pleasure
spending time with you.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:29.451
Actually, l was hoping

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.990
we might do this sort
of thing more often.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:34.794
Hmm.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.056
We're passing
through a subspace eddy.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.189
lt could be the wake
of another ship.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.323
No.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.799
There's nothing on sensors.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.960
lt's probably
just the gravimetric shear

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.298
from the nebula.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.373
Maybe l should
take the controls.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.135
Sit down and relax,
Captain.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:52.042
You've got a hologram
at the helm.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.790
The plasma surges
have to be coming

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.296
from one of these relays.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:56.199
Try realigning the
deuterium manifolds.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:00.804
Paris to Torres.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.238
Go ahead.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:05.210
Can you pull yourself away from
Engineering for a few minutes?

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.644
l've got a shuttle down here
with faulty deflector array.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.238
l'm a little busy right now.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.579
lt's kind of urgent.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.522
What's this?

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.997
Well, l thought you'd enjoy
a romantic lunch

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.034
under the glow of a red giant.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:33.732
Oh, you replicated potato salad.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.604
With extra paprika--
just the way you like it.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:41.443
This is so sweet... but l can't.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.947
Sure you can.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:46.110
l've already cleared it
with Chakotay.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.086
l told the Captain l'd
have the dilithium matrix

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.123
recalibrated
before she got back.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.954
You know, this might be
our last chance

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:59.932
to be alone...
for the next 18 years.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.398
l will make some time

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.902
before the baby
comes, l promise.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:09.575
Oh, l've got to get back.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.214
Report.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.380
There's some kind
of pulse being directed

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.390
at our transceiver array.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.551
lt's coming
from the Delta Flyer.

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.891
Hail them.

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.896
No response.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.797
Looks like they've encoded
the pulse with a com signal.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.637
Captain...

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:41.333
Sorry about the image, Ensign.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:42.772
Our com system's been damaged.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.104
The only way
l could send you a signal

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.610
was through the main deflector.

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.669
Are you and the Doctor
all right?

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:48.941
We're fine.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:50.676
Tell Commander Chakotay
to meet me in my ready room

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.944
as soon as we've docked.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.610
Janeway out.

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.550
Harry tells me the Flyer
took some damage.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:58.954
That's an understatement.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:01.050
We almost didn't
make it back in one piece.

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.027
They're called the R'Kaal.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:05.826
Their technology is
decades ahead of ours.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.490
Transphasic warp drive,

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.660
multispectral
cloaking systems.

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:10.667
They could destroy
this ship

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.829
before our sensors
knew they were there.

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:14.372
They sound like people
we should avoid.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.498
l wish that were possible.

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:17.371
They control
thousands of parsecs

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.968
from here to the edge
of the Beta Quadrant.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.570
They're ecological extremists.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:24.514
They believe conventional
warp engines damage subspace,

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:27.576
so they've outlawed warp travel
through their territory.

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.883
Then we should reverse course
and find a way around.

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.546
That's the problem.

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:32.682
We've already been
in their space

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.693
for three weeks
without knowing it.

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:36.558
You'd think they'd mark
their borders

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.893
-a little more clearly.
-As punishment,

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:42.662
their law demands
that our ship be dismantled.

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:45.499
Obviously, we're not going
to let that happen.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.732
l spent three hours
explaining our situation

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.398
to their ''Supreme Archon''--

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:51.602
a thoroughly unpleasant man.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.941
l convinced him
to spare Voyager,

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.241
but at a price.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:59.341
We're going to rendezvous
with their armada

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:01.512
and surrender our warp core

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:05.353
at a Class-M planet where
they've agreed to let us settle.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:06.619
Settle?

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:09.183
l didn't make this decision
lightly, Chakotay.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.560
We have to bring
the senior staff in on this.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.531
We can find a way
to evade their ships

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:16.193
or adapt our sensors
to their cloaking technology.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.735
We could try that,

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.169
and we might make it
past their armada,

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:21.069
but we could lose a lot
of people in the process--

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.198
maybe the entire ship.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:23.570
Kathyrn, there's got
to be another way.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:26.874
l'm tired, Chakotay,
tired of casualty reports,

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:29.243
of continually risking my people
on the slim chance

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:31.044
that we'll make it home
in one piece.

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:35.086
We've found our way
out of worse situations.

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.587
Set a course.

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.180
What am l supposed
to tell the crew?

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:40.418
For now, l'd like
to keep this between us.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:42.757
lt's not like you to keep
your people in the dark...

00:07:42.829 --> 00:07:44.421
l'll make an announcement
when the time is right.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.260
Dismissed.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.307
Captain.

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:58.809
l'm sorry to interrupt,

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:02.211
but l could use your input
on a hypothetical scenario.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.213
Of course.

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.716
lf we were to eject the core,

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:08.549
could it be
towed safely at warp?

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:11.181
ln theory, but a tractor beam

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:12.690
might destabilize
the containment field.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.055
You'd be risking a breach.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.821
Could you compensate
for that?

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.361
You could configure
the tractor emitters

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.022
to generate a resonance pulse.

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:21.066
That should stabilize the field.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.192
Can you make those
modifications

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.770
to the Delta Flyer's
tractor emitters?

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:26.839
l suppose.

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:29.531
How long would it take?

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:31.007
Um, a few hours.

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:32.806
Get started.

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:34.870
l thought you said this was
a hypothetical scenario.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.244
We should be prepared,
just in case.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:38.874
ln case of what?

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:42.113
Let me know as soon
as you're finished.

00:08:44.991 --> 00:08:46.754
Torres to Chakotay.

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:48.088
Go ahead.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.822
Have you got a minute?

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:13.619
B'Elanna tells me you ordered
some modifications to the Flyer.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.415
That's right.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:16.682
Maybe l misunderstood.

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:18.815
l thought the plan was
to hand over the core

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.950
when we reached the planet.

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:23.689
Are we taking it somewhere else?

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.822
l heard you the first time.

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:27.297
Captain?

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:31.359
You've already made
your concerns clear, Commander,

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.495
but there's been
a slight change of plans.

00:09:33.606 --> 00:09:35.164
Were you going to tell me?

00:09:37.276 --> 00:09:38.675
Kathryn...

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:41.235
what's going on?

00:09:41.314 --> 00:09:42.679
l don't feel well.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:44.648
l've got a headache.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:47.583
l'm going to my quarters,

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:49.746
and l'd prefer
not to be disturbed.

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:51.119
You have the Bridge.

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:55.159
Not now.

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:56.353
l beg your pardon, Captain?

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:58.294
Carry on, Commander.

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:10.804
Chakotay to the Doctor.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:12.138
Go ahead, Commander.

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:14.179
Report to Sick Bay immediately.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.642
Something wrong
with the turbolifts?

00:10:19.719 --> 00:10:21.949
You did say immediately.
How can l help you?

00:10:22.054 --> 00:10:23.646
l'm concerned
about the Captain.

00:10:23.723 --> 00:10:25.156
She doesn't seem
to be feeling well.

00:10:25.224 --> 00:10:26.156
What's wrong?

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:27.157
l'm not sure.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:29.160
She went to her quarters
with a headache.

00:10:29.228 --> 00:10:31.662
l'll bring her an analgesic.

00:10:31.731 --> 00:10:33.323
l was wondering if
this could be related

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:34.957
to your encounter
with the aliens.

00:10:35.101 --> 00:10:36.159
You think they harmed her?

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:37.701
You tell me.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.237
What did they do to her?

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:41.364
l'm not sure, exactly.

00:10:41.474 --> 00:10:43.203
The aliens took
my program off-line

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:44.936
as soon as they boarded
the Flyer.

00:10:45.011 --> 00:10:46.911
The Captain reactivated
me a few hours later

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.241
and told me she'd
been interrogated.

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:50.373
Naturally, l examined her
to make sure she was all right.

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.883
Did you find
anything unusual?

00:10:52.952 --> 00:10:55.716
l suppose l'm violating
doctor-patient confidentiality

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:58.882
by telling you this,
but... she was fine.

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:01.620
l'd like you to give her
a more thorough examination.

00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:04.356
Gladly, but you know
how she feels about physicals.

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.159
You can be very persuasive,
Doctor.

00:11:06.232 --> 00:11:07.893
Contact me as soon
as you're done.

00:11:08.034 --> 00:11:09.899
Aye, sir.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.900
Anything interesting on sensors
this morning?

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.304
Nothing extraordinary.

00:11:18.377 --> 00:11:20.641
A red giant
and two G-type stars,

00:11:20.713 --> 00:11:25.309
a Golorian trading vessel
bearing 156 mark 4.

00:11:25.384 --> 00:11:27.318
lf there were a fleet
of cloaked ships

00:11:27.386 --> 00:11:29.946
in the vicinity, could you
devise a way to detect them?

00:11:30.022 --> 00:11:31.614
A cloaked fleet
would generate

00:11:31.691 --> 00:11:33.488
significant subspace
distortions.

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:34.821
Why do you ask?

00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:37.954
Commander, we're receiving
a transmission.

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:39.156
Source?

00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:40.960
l'm having trouble
pinpointing it.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.499
Should l notify the Captain?

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:44.535
No, she didn't want
to be disturbed.

00:11:44.603 --> 00:11:47.504
Route the call here.

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:50.474
l'm Commander Chakotay
of the Starship Voyager.

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:53.979
This is Supreme Archon Loth
of the R'Kaal lmperium.

00:11:54.113 --> 00:11:55.876
Why haven't you ejected
your warp core

00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:57.882
as your Captain agreed?

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.316
We're en route to the planet
you specified.

00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:02.854
We can't jettison the core
until we get there.

00:12:02.922 --> 00:12:06.255
lf we don't receive the core
within ten hours,

00:12:06.325 --> 00:12:09.886
my armada will destroy
your ship.

00:12:09.995 --> 00:12:13.556
This is your only warning.

00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:16.599
Work with Harry.

00:12:16.702 --> 00:12:19.136
l want to know the source
of that transmission.

00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:21.002
Understood.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.940
Ah, Commander,
you'll be relieved to know

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:29.572
l've given the Captain
a clean bill of health.

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:31.138
Did you run a
neurological scan?

00:12:31.217 --> 00:12:33.811
Mm-hmm. Her brain activity
and cognitive functions

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:34.944
are completely normal.

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:36.646
As far as l can tell,
she's perfectly fit,

00:12:36.722 --> 00:12:38.952
physically and mentally.

00:12:39.058 --> 00:12:40.855
Thank you, Doctor.

00:12:50.569 --> 00:12:52.366
Chakotay to the Captain.

00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:56.006
Computer,
locate Captain Janeway.

00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:57.006
Computer, belay that.

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:58.736
My quarters, now.

00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:01.637
Really, Chakotay,

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:04.080
sending the Doctor
to check up on me?

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.412
l'm concerned.

00:13:05.484 --> 00:13:06.883
Then why didn't you come
to me directly?

00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:08.248
l thought we trusted each other.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.252
So did l.

00:13:09.321 --> 00:13:11.084
Something happened
on that away mission

00:13:11.157 --> 00:13:12.089
that you're not telling me.

00:13:12.158 --> 00:13:14.092
l've told you everything
you need to know.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.752
You've consulted me
on every major decision

00:13:15.828 --> 00:13:18.422
over the last seven
years except this one.

00:13:18.497 --> 00:13:20.089
Why?

00:13:20.166 --> 00:13:21.326
There are some decisions

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.766
a captain has to make
on her own.

00:13:23.869 --> 00:13:25.894
l understand that,
but every instinct

00:13:26.038 --> 00:13:28.438
tells me what you're
doing is wrong.

00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:30.907
Don't you remember
what happened on Lessek Prime?

00:13:31.977 --> 00:13:34.070
l don't see how
that's relevant.

00:13:34.146 --> 00:13:35.408
l think you do.

00:13:35.481 --> 00:13:37.415
15 years ago,
you were the Lieutenant

00:13:37.483 --> 00:13:38.814
who was kept in the dark.

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:41.352
lf you hadn't questioned
your Captain's orders,

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.650
the entire away team
would've been lost.

00:13:44.723 --> 00:13:47.692
This situation's
entirely different.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:50.251
You never told me that story.

00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:51.421
l made it up.

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:53.158
Chakotay to Tuvok.

00:13:53.232 --> 00:13:55.666
l've erected a dampening field

00:13:55.734 --> 00:13:57.599
around these quarters.

00:13:57.703 --> 00:13:59.671
l'm sorry, Commander.

00:14:15.654 --> 00:14:17.747
Computer, secure the doors
and establish

00:14:17.823 --> 00:14:21.919
a level-5 dampening field
around the morgue.

00:14:49.355 --> 00:14:51.323
l can't do my job
with the two of you

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.688
constantly talking in my head.

00:14:59.164 --> 00:15:01.189
No!

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:05.600
l'm not doing anything else
until l speak with the Captain.

00:15:08.974 --> 00:15:10.874
Fine!

00:15:10.976 --> 00:15:14.173
What's your
encryption frequency?

00:15:15.247 --> 00:15:17.613
Captain, are you all right?

00:15:17.683 --> 00:15:19.116
Doctor, listen to me.

00:15:19.184 --> 00:15:23.018
Under no circumstances
are you to eject the warp core.

00:15:23.088 --> 00:15:25.181
lf l don't do what they ask,
they'll kill you.

00:15:25.257 --> 00:15:27.122
l'm giving you a direct order.

00:15:27.192 --> 00:15:28.625
Stop what you're doing.

00:15:28.694 --> 00:15:29.888
l'm sorry, Captain.

00:15:29.995 --> 00:15:31.690
l can't obey that order.

00:15:31.764 --> 00:15:33.698
Doctor, l want you
to go to the Bridge right now

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:34.892
and alert Commander Tuvok...

00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:36.626
Put her behind
the force field!

00:15:42.207 --> 00:15:44.607
We have another assignment
for you.

00:15:44.677 --> 00:15:47.942
l've been going over
the schematics of your vessel,

00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:52.039
and l'm intrigued
by this bio-neural circuitry.

00:15:52.117 --> 00:15:55.644
l want you to bring us
a series of these gel packs.

00:15:55.721 --> 00:15:58.952
The gel packs are integrated
into the ship's systems.

00:15:59.058 --> 00:16:00.992
l can't just remove them
without someone noticing.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:04.029
You've proven yourself to be
very resourceful, Doctor.

00:16:04.096 --> 00:16:05.529
You'll find a way.

00:16:05.597 --> 00:16:06.791
Remember--

00:16:06.865 --> 00:16:09.698
we're monitoring
your perceptual subroutines.

00:16:09.802 --> 00:16:14.171
We can see and hear everything.

00:16:15.841 --> 00:16:17.206
Tuvok to Chakotay.

00:16:17.276 --> 00:16:20.541
You know what will happen to her
if you alert your crew.

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:26.444
Go ahead.

00:16:26.518 --> 00:16:28.713
Are you all right, Commander?

00:16:28.787 --> 00:16:29.879
Uh, just a scratchy throat.

00:16:30.022 --> 00:16:31.284
The Doctor's treating me now.

00:16:31.357 --> 00:16:32.881
Could you come
to the Shuttle Bay

00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:34.084
when you're finished?

00:16:34.159 --> 00:16:35.251
l'll be right there.

00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:36.794
Chakotay out.

00:16:39.164 --> 00:16:41.291
Computer,
access the holodeck database

00:16:41.367 --> 00:16:44.393
and locate Commander Chakotay's
holographic template.

00:16:44.503 --> 00:16:47.336
Download the physical parameters
into my program.

00:17:07.593 --> 00:17:09.185
You wanted to see me?

00:17:09.261 --> 00:17:11.821
l've completed the diagnostic
as you requested.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:14.364
The Flyer's com system
is functioning normally.

00:17:14.433 --> 00:17:15.695
You find that unusual?

00:17:15.768 --> 00:17:18.828
The Captain did report
that it was damaged

00:17:19.004 --> 00:17:20.471
during the attack
by the R'Kaal.

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:21.699
l'll have a talk with her.

00:17:21.807 --> 00:17:24.241
Did you find anything else
out of the ordinary?

00:17:24.309 --> 00:17:25.435
No.

00:17:25.511 --> 00:17:28.071
Get out of there
before you arouse suspicion.

00:17:28.147 --> 00:17:30.707
l'll be on the Bridge
if you need me.

00:17:32.885 --> 00:17:35.012
You're doing
a wonderful job, Doctor.

00:17:37.656 --> 00:17:39.817
l'm just giving him
a little encouragement.

00:17:39.892 --> 00:17:42.588
That's why l'm in command.

00:17:50.035 --> 00:17:51.525
lf all goes well, we should have

00:17:51.637 --> 00:17:53.468
the warp core
in less than six hours.

00:17:53.539 --> 00:17:55.097
He's making excellent progress.

00:17:55.207 --> 00:17:58.472
That's exactly what
he wants you to believe.

00:17:58.544 --> 00:17:59.568
What do you mean?

00:17:59.645 --> 00:18:03.103
Did you really think
you could outsmart a hologram?

00:18:06.585 --> 00:18:08.576
Everything appears to be normal.

00:18:08.654 --> 00:18:09.814
How do you know
you're not looking

00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:11.822
at a holographic projection?

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:14.415
The Doctor isn't
just a physician.

00:18:14.493 --> 00:18:16.552
His emergency command
subroutines

00:18:16.628 --> 00:18:19.222
contain thousands
of tactical scenarios.

00:18:19.298 --> 00:18:20.765
l wouldn't be surprised

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:23.358
if Voyager was already
on its way here.

00:18:23.469 --> 00:18:26.063
You do have an option.

00:18:26.171 --> 00:18:28.435
Leave me behind
in an escape pod,

00:18:28.507 --> 00:18:31.408
and l'll forget
any of this ever happened.

00:18:32.478 --> 00:18:34.878
Maybe we should let her go.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.777
Are you delusional?

00:18:36.849 --> 00:18:39.545
lt took months to plan this.

00:18:39.618 --> 00:18:42.018
We've already found a buyer
for the warp core.

00:18:42.087 --> 00:18:43.884
Now you want
to abandon everything?

00:18:43.956 --> 00:18:46.686
lt's better than being sent
to a rehabilitation center.

00:18:46.758 --> 00:18:50.421
We made our choice
when we stole this vessel.

00:18:50.496 --> 00:18:52.054
l am not going back

00:18:52.131 --> 00:18:54.122
to the Hierarchy,
and neither are you.

00:18:58.637 --> 00:19:01.538
She's just trying to trick you.

00:19:02.574 --> 00:19:04.633
A month from now,

00:19:04.743 --> 00:19:09.180
we'll be soaking
in the mud baths of Eblar Prime.

00:19:09.248 --> 00:19:11.546
Trust me.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.818
Janeway to Torres.

00:19:19.925 --> 00:19:21.017
Torres here.

00:19:21.093 --> 00:19:23.084
l'm having a little trouble
with my replicator again.

00:19:23.162 --> 00:19:24.288
Can you take a look at it?

00:19:24.363 --> 00:19:26.490
l'm still working on those
modifications you asked for.

00:19:26.565 --> 00:19:27.497
l'll send somebody else.

00:19:27.566 --> 00:19:29.124
l'd consider it a personal favor

00:19:29.234 --> 00:19:30.963
if you'd do it yourself,
Lieutenant.

00:19:31.069 --> 00:19:32.627
l'll be there in five minutes.

00:19:32.738 --> 00:19:33.705
Thank you.

00:19:33.772 --> 00:19:34.932
Janeway out.

00:19:38.076 --> 00:19:41.011
Computer, access Lieutenant
Torres' holographic template

00:19:41.079 --> 00:19:42.512
and download
the physical parameters

00:19:42.581 --> 00:19:44.208
into my program.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:58.855
Computer, access
medical file: Torres-3

00:19:58.931 --> 00:20:01.729
and update
her holographic template.

00:20:26.992 --> 00:20:29.756
Did you forget something,
Lieutenant?

00:20:29.828 --> 00:20:31.762
l did, actually.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.458
Where do we keep
the spare gel packs?

00:20:36.034 --> 00:20:37.262
Locker Gamma 5.

00:20:37.369 --> 00:20:40.167
Of course, Gamma 5.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.808
On the upper level.

00:20:43.909 --> 00:20:45.774
l know where it is, Ensign.

00:20:56.989 --> 00:20:58.820
You left me no choice.

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.380
Lieutenant.

00:21:00.492 --> 00:21:02.517
Oh, are we calling each other
by our rank now?

00:21:04.596 --> 00:21:05.824
Uh, you startled me.

00:21:05.897 --> 00:21:07.194
Oh, sorry.

00:21:07.266 --> 00:21:09.734
Well, l thought
since you didn't have time

00:21:09.835 --> 00:21:11.302
for lunch under the stars,

00:21:11.403 --> 00:21:14.372
maybe you'd settle for
the glow of the warp core.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.533
How thoughtful...

00:21:17.643 --> 00:21:20.840
but l'm... not hungry.

00:21:20.912 --> 00:21:23.540
Well, l'm sure the
baby is famished.

00:21:23.615 --> 00:21:27.107
A pregnant woman
shouldn't eat this kind of food.

00:21:27.185 --> 00:21:28.880
Do you want to give me
an arterial occlusion?

00:21:28.954 --> 00:21:32.287
Oh, one drumstick
isn't going to kill you.

00:21:32.357 --> 00:21:35.793
Besides, l won't
tell the Doctor...

00:21:35.861 --> 00:21:37.590
if you won't.

00:21:37.663 --> 00:21:39.858
You know...

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:41.626
this all looks so delicious.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:42.860
Why don't we save it

00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:44.925
for a romantic dinner
this evening?

00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:47.335
All right.

00:21:47.406 --> 00:21:49.374
1900 hours, but if
you're not there,

00:21:49.474 --> 00:21:51.237
l'm sending Security after you.

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:54.108
l'll be there... sweetheart.

00:21:54.179 --> 00:21:56.443
''Sweetheart''?

00:21:56.515 --> 00:21:58.506
Well, aren't you
getting affectionate

00:21:58.583 --> 00:22:00.210
in your third trimester.

00:22:07.125 --> 00:22:09.252
l'll see you later.

00:22:20.005 --> 00:22:21.267
Kim to Chakotay.

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:22.898
Can you come to Astrometrics?

00:22:23.041 --> 00:22:25.066
Harry, l'll be right there.

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:27.737
Chakotay out.

00:22:32.617 --> 00:22:35.051
The transmission was encoded
with a false subspace signature.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.384
The signal didn't originate
on another vessel.

00:22:37.456 --> 00:22:39.424
lt came from inside Voyager.

00:22:39.491 --> 00:22:42.085
We traced it to Holodeck 2.

00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:43.718
Do you know who sent it?

00:22:43.795 --> 00:22:45.387
l'm on my way
to check the access logs.

00:22:45.464 --> 00:22:47.591
l'll go with you.

00:22:48.834 --> 00:22:50.426
Whoever sent this transmission

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:52.059
knew how to cover his tracks.

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:54.001
The holodeck logs
have been erased.

00:22:54.072 --> 00:22:56.472
Doesn't look like
we'll get any answers here.

00:22:56.541 --> 00:22:57.769
l might be able to find

00:22:57.843 --> 00:23:00.243
some residual
photonic displacement.

00:23:01.947 --> 00:23:04.279
There we go.

00:23:04.349 --> 00:23:05.281
l think l can clarify
the image

00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:07.477
with a recursive algorithm.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:10.715
Our alien's a hologram.

00:23:10.789 --> 00:23:12.381
The question is,
who programmed him?

00:23:12.457 --> 00:23:13.389
Good work, Ensign.

00:23:13.458 --> 00:23:14.550
l'll take it from here.

00:23:14.626 --> 00:23:15.888
Wait a minute.

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:18.361
l'm picking up
two holographic signatures.

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:20.990
lt looks like a second image
was superimposed

00:23:21.066 --> 00:23:22.590
over an existing template.

00:23:22.701 --> 00:23:25.932
l'll see if l can isolate
the first image.

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:19.279
Doctor...

00:24:19.357 --> 00:24:20.881
what are you doing?

00:24:20.959 --> 00:24:23.393
lf you don't mind,

00:24:23.462 --> 00:24:26.829
l've had a stressful day.

00:24:31.603 --> 00:24:32.797
l'm extremely busy, Commander.

00:24:32.904 --> 00:24:35.202
This will only take a moment.

00:24:35.273 --> 00:24:37.935
l've been reviewing
the communication logs.

00:24:38.076 --> 00:24:40.874
There's a discrepancy
l was hoping you could explain.

00:24:40.946 --> 00:24:44.438
At the precise moment the Flyer
transmitted a deflector pulse,

00:24:44.516 --> 00:24:47.542
you apparently accessed
Voyager's holographic database.

00:24:49.421 --> 00:24:52.447
l haven't the faintest idea
what you're talking about.

00:24:52.524 --> 00:24:54.458
Your access code was used

00:24:54.526 --> 00:24:58.121
to download the Captain's
physical parameters.

00:24:58.196 --> 00:25:00.687
Exactly what are
you insinuating, Commander?

00:25:00.765 --> 00:25:03.199
Perhaps we should have a word
with the Captain.

00:25:03.301 --> 00:25:04.268
Fine.

00:25:07.506 --> 00:25:09.474
Computer, deactivate the EMH.

00:25:09.574 --> 00:25:12.168
EMH protocols are off-line.

00:25:12.244 --> 00:25:15.270
Security to Sick Bay.
Remain where you are.

00:25:15.347 --> 00:25:16.541
You haven't forgotten

00:25:16.615 --> 00:25:17.980
l'm a hologram, have you?

00:25:21.620 --> 00:25:24.316
lf necessary, l'll disable
all of your holo-emitters.

00:25:28.627 --> 00:25:32.188
Computer, transfer the EMH
to the mobile emitter!

00:25:32.264 --> 00:25:34.232
All hands, Red Alert.

00:25:34.299 --> 00:25:36.062
Security teams,
apprehend the Doctor.

00:25:42.307 --> 00:25:44.571
Computer,
open the holodeck doors.

00:25:44.643 --> 00:25:45.940
Unable to comply.

00:25:46.011 --> 00:25:48.206
Access to the holodeck
has been restricted.

00:25:48.280 --> 00:25:51.147
Security override:
Tuvok-sigma-four.

00:25:54.753 --> 00:25:56.618
Computer, end program.

00:25:56.688 --> 00:25:58.952
Unable to comply.

00:25:59.090 --> 00:26:01.285
Holodeck controls are off-line.

00:26:01.393 --> 00:26:03.020
Tuvok to Engineering.

00:26:03.061 --> 00:26:04.289
Shut down power to Holodeck 2.

00:26:04.362 --> 00:26:05.454
Shut down power to Holodeck 2.

00:26:06.798 --> 00:26:08.993
lt looks like the Doctor's
rerouted the power relays.

00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:10.829
lt'll take a minute
to bypass them.

00:26:11.002 --> 00:26:13.562
Doctor, l've reconfigured
my phaser

00:26:13.672 --> 00:26:16.266
to disrupt your holo-matrix.

00:26:16.374 --> 00:26:18.865
Surrender yourself now.

00:26:28.520 --> 00:26:30.078
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:26:30.155 --> 00:26:32.487
Can you locate the Doctor
on internal sensors?

00:26:32.557 --> 00:26:33.888
l'm not reading him.

00:26:33.992 --> 00:26:36.722
He must've masked
his signature somehow.

00:26:36.795 --> 00:26:38.820
Try scanning for the
polydeutonic alloy

00:26:38.897 --> 00:26:39.829
in his emitter.

00:26:39.898 --> 00:26:42.298
Shut down all turbolifts
and transporters.

00:26:42.367 --> 00:26:44.528
Acknowledged.

00:26:44.669 --> 00:26:47.103
Get your people out of here.

00:26:47.172 --> 00:26:48.230
The core's about to breach.

00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:50.399
l'm not detecting an overload.

00:26:50.508 --> 00:26:51.941
You're getting false readings.

00:26:52.010 --> 00:26:54.274
The Doctor's reprogrammed
your sensors.

00:26:54.346 --> 00:26:56.280
All right, everybody out!

00:26:56.348 --> 00:26:58.873
Now! Move it!

00:26:58.950 --> 00:26:59.939
You, too, B'Elanna.

00:27:00.018 --> 00:27:02.816
l might be able to stabilize
the containment field.

00:27:02.887 --> 00:27:05.481
You're not putting
your baby in danger. Go!

00:27:05.557 --> 00:27:06.956
You'd better be right behind me.

00:27:07.025 --> 00:27:08.458
Paris to Torres.

00:27:08.526 --> 00:27:10.494
l'm picking up the Doctor's
emitter in your section.

00:27:10.562 --> 00:27:11.654
Where?

00:27:11.730 --> 00:27:13.425
Right next to the warp core.

00:27:27.012 --> 00:27:28.445
Computer...

00:27:28.513 --> 00:27:31.038
activate Emergency
Command Hologram.

00:27:32.584 --> 00:27:35.246
All command codes have been
transferred to the ECH.

00:27:35.320 --> 00:27:36.719
Prepare to eject the warp core.

00:27:36.788 --> 00:27:41.225
Authorization:
ECH-omega-four-two.

00:27:41.292 --> 00:27:43.226
Doctor, don't do this.

00:27:43.294 --> 00:27:45.421
Warp ejection system enabled.

00:27:45.497 --> 00:27:47.624
Computer... eject the core.

00:27:53.505 --> 00:27:54.437
Computer,

00:27:54.506 --> 00:27:55.598
lock on to my mobile emitter

00:27:55.707 --> 00:27:57.436
and transport me
to the Delta Flyer.

00:27:57.509 --> 00:27:59.568
Transporters are off-line.

00:28:02.580 --> 00:28:04.639
Tuvok, we just lost main power,

00:28:04.716 --> 00:28:06.547
and internal sensors are down.

00:28:06.618 --> 00:28:10.782
The Doctor has entered
Jefferies Tube 1 1-Alpha.

00:28:10.855 --> 00:28:13.483
Send a security team
to the Shuttle Bay.

00:28:24.969 --> 00:28:26.436
Lieutenant.

00:28:26.504 --> 00:28:29.268
l think the Doctor's heading
for the escape pods.

00:28:32.644 --> 00:28:35.875
You wouldn't shoot
a pregnant woman, would you?

00:28:35.980 --> 00:28:37.447
Come with me, Doctor.

00:28:49.794 --> 00:28:53.423
Tuvok, someone's launching
the Flyer.

00:28:53.498 --> 00:28:55.966
Tuvok?

00:29:12.550 --> 00:29:14.814
Ow!

00:29:21.893 --> 00:29:26.193
You might try disconnecting
the phase discriminator.

00:29:33.138 --> 00:29:35.197
l've rebuilt
dozens of these units,

00:29:35.306 --> 00:29:37.706
but l've never seen
this configuration before.

00:29:37.776 --> 00:29:39.744
Do you know how l can stabilize
the ion flow?

00:29:45.250 --> 00:29:48.242
That looks like
the charge inverter.

00:29:50.655 --> 00:29:52.145
Thank you.

00:29:52.223 --> 00:29:53.212
You're welcome.

00:29:53.291 --> 00:29:55.725
Your ship must need
a lot of replacement parts.

00:29:55.794 --> 00:29:58.763
Oh... those aren't
for this ship.

00:29:58.830 --> 00:30:00.821
l've been collecting
and repairing

00:30:00.899 --> 00:30:02.560
spare components for years.

00:30:02.634 --> 00:30:05.125
This is from an
old impulse drive.

00:30:05.203 --> 00:30:07.694
Would you believe l found it
sitting in a waste depository?

00:30:07.806 --> 00:30:09.899
l'll be able to find a buyer
now that it's working.

00:30:10.074 --> 00:30:12.269
These parts could be worth
a small fortune.

00:30:12.343 --> 00:30:15.312
That's exactly what l think.

00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:17.940
l'm going to use
my quarter of the profits

00:30:18.082 --> 00:30:19.310
to establish an outpost

00:30:19.384 --> 00:30:21.784
specializing in obsolete
engine components.

00:30:21.853 --> 00:30:23.753
l'm certain
there's a demand for them.

00:30:23.822 --> 00:30:26.120
My Chief Engineer is always
looking for spare parts.

00:30:26.191 --> 00:30:27.283
She might be interested

00:30:27.358 --> 00:30:29.292
in acquiring
your entire inventory.

00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:30.884
Captain.

00:30:33.164 --> 00:30:35.189
You're not trying
to take advantage

00:30:35.266 --> 00:30:36.858
of my subordinate, are you?

00:30:38.636 --> 00:30:41.799
No one's ever going
to buy this junk.

00:30:41.906 --> 00:30:43.897
lt's almost as useless as you.

00:30:45.143 --> 00:30:46.872
There's a ship approaching.

00:30:50.081 --> 00:30:51.173
This is the Delta Flyer.

00:30:51.249 --> 00:30:52.716
l've got the warp core,

00:30:52.784 --> 00:30:55.252
but you're not getting it
until you release the Captain.

00:31:01.025 --> 00:31:02.720
Are you insane?

00:31:02.794 --> 00:31:05.024
You almost destabilized
the core.

00:31:05.096 --> 00:31:06.586
Both of our ships
would've been destroyed!

00:31:06.664 --> 00:31:08.393
This isn't a negotiation!

00:31:08.466 --> 00:31:10.696
Release your tractor beam now!

00:31:10.802 --> 00:31:13.270
All right.

00:31:18.176 --> 00:31:20.610
lt's in the Cargo Hold.

00:31:20.678 --> 00:31:24.409
Lower your shields, and we'll
beam your Captain to you.

00:31:27.685 --> 00:31:29.084
Ready.

00:31:32.557 --> 00:31:34.650
We had an agreement.

00:31:34.726 --> 00:31:38.184
To spare your Captain.

00:31:38.263 --> 00:31:40.754
As you can see,
she's still alive.

00:31:40.832 --> 00:31:43.130
Let the Doctor go.
l'm the more valuable hostage.

00:31:43.234 --> 00:31:44.826
Actually, you're not.

00:31:44.936 --> 00:31:47.632
We'll leave you
in the Vinri system.

00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:50.503
The inhabitants are
mostly harmless.

00:31:50.575 --> 00:31:52.805
The Doctor will be working
for us now.

00:31:52.877 --> 00:31:54.504
l'll do no such thing.

00:31:54.579 --> 00:31:56.342
l'm sure you'll feel differently

00:31:56.414 --> 00:31:59.872
after l make a few adjustments
to your program.

00:32:04.022 --> 00:32:06.320
l had no idea
he was going to do this.

00:32:06.391 --> 00:32:09.417
l'm sorry.

00:32:09.494 --> 00:32:12.691
l hope you realize
you've stranded Voyager

00:32:12.764 --> 00:32:13.890
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:32:13.965 --> 00:32:15.865
What did you expect me to do,
let them kill you?

00:32:15.934 --> 00:32:18.425
l expected you
to follow my orders.

00:32:18.536 --> 00:32:19.935
You might as well
have been ordering me

00:32:20.004 --> 00:32:21.096
to put a phaser to your head.

00:32:21.205 --> 00:32:23.537
Voyager can survive

00:32:23.608 --> 00:32:26.372
without a warp core,
but not without a captain.

00:32:26.444 --> 00:32:29.777
Now it doesn't have either.

00:32:37.188 --> 00:32:43.286
Chief Tactical Officer's Log,
Stardate 54890.7.

00:32:43.361 --> 00:32:45.295
With internal sensors off-line,

00:32:45.363 --> 00:32:47.957
l've had to order
a section-by-section search

00:32:48.032 --> 00:32:49.795
for our missing crew members.

00:32:49.867 --> 00:32:51.960
Until main power is restored,

00:32:52.070 --> 00:32:56.006
Voyager remains immobilized
and defenseless.

00:33:09.287 --> 00:33:11.050
They're just unconscious.

00:33:11.122 --> 00:33:13.215
Paris to Tuvok.

00:33:13.291 --> 00:33:14.883
l found them.

00:33:14.993 --> 00:33:16.426
lt is logical to assume

00:33:16.494 --> 00:33:18.553
the Captain never returned
from the away mission.

00:33:18.629 --> 00:33:20.620
Do you have any idea
where the Flyer is?

00:33:20.698 --> 00:33:23.189
The Doctor masked his ion trail.

00:33:23.301 --> 00:33:25.292
Engineering to Chakotay.

00:33:25.403 --> 00:33:26.335
Go ahead.

00:33:26.404 --> 00:33:28.065
We're ready to restart
the impulse reactors.

00:33:28.172 --> 00:33:29.639
Acknowledged.

00:33:54.365 --> 00:33:57.823
lt's playing on every
com channel on the ship.

00:33:57.902 --> 00:33:59.529
Computer, pause music.

00:33:59.637 --> 00:34:02.367
Unable to comply.

00:34:02.473 --> 00:34:04.464
Didn't the Doctor play this
at his recital last month?

00:34:04.542 --> 00:34:06.009
Yes, and as l recall,

00:34:06.077 --> 00:34:08.568
he performed the piece
flawlessly.

00:34:08.646 --> 00:34:11.638
Maybe the recording was
damaged by the power loss.

00:34:11.716 --> 00:34:15.083
Or perhaps the Doctor altered
the music deliberately.

00:34:15.153 --> 00:34:17.144
Why would he do that?

00:34:17.221 --> 00:34:19.655
l performed a Fourier analysis
on the recording.

00:34:19.724 --> 00:34:21.419
The harmonics have been
modified.

00:34:21.492 --> 00:34:23.221
it could be a com frequency.

00:34:23.294 --> 00:34:25.057
Unlikely.
There's no carrier wave.

00:34:25.129 --> 00:34:28.257
l could be wrong, but it looks
like a warp signature.

00:34:28.332 --> 00:34:30.391
The power utilization curve
would be about right.

00:34:30.501 --> 00:34:32.025
Try scanning for it.

00:34:33.971 --> 00:34:36.439
l'm detecting
a matching signature.

00:34:36.541 --> 00:34:38.941
Distance: 6.7 light-years.

00:34:39.043 --> 00:34:41.876
We can't follow them at impulse.

00:34:41.946 --> 00:34:44.005
You and Tom take a shuttle.

00:34:58.563 --> 00:34:59.860
What are you doing?

00:34:59.931 --> 00:35:01.455
lf l can amplify your matrix,

00:35:01.566 --> 00:35:04.194
l might be able to disrupt
the force field.

00:35:06.537 --> 00:35:09.870
l'm sorry l put us in
this position, Captain.

00:35:10.007 --> 00:35:12.100
You said you wanted us
to spend more time together.

00:35:12.176 --> 00:35:15.771
This isn't what
l had in mind.

00:35:15.847 --> 00:35:19.339
Maybe... if we get
back to the ship,

00:35:19.417 --> 00:35:21.510
we could try socializing
a little more.

00:35:21.586 --> 00:35:25.147
This really isn't the place
to be talking about this.

00:35:25.223 --> 00:35:27.885
Besides, l don't do
a lot of socializing.

00:35:28.025 --> 00:35:30.653
You have meals with
Commander Chakotay,

00:35:30.728 --> 00:35:32.662
and you play
velocity with Seven.

00:35:32.730 --> 00:35:35.290
We going to have
to discuss this later.

00:35:35.366 --> 00:35:37.664
l need to upload
your first assignment.

00:35:48.479 --> 00:35:50.276
You want me to infiltrate

00:35:50.348 --> 00:35:52.680
the Hierarchy's
surveillance complex?

00:35:52.750 --> 00:35:55.082
The data stored there is
worth a hundred warp cores.

00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:57.678
How do you expect me to get past
their security perimeter?

00:35:57.755 --> 00:35:59.723
l'm glad you asked.

00:36:05.663 --> 00:36:07.722
l trust this won't be permanent?

00:36:07.798 --> 00:36:10.460
l've given you the rank
of a Class-One Overseer.

00:36:10.568 --> 00:36:12.160
You'll be able to walk
into Central Command

00:36:12.270 --> 00:36:13.202
without anyone noticing.

00:36:13.271 --> 00:36:14.203
l've also uploaded

00:36:14.272 --> 00:36:15.364
several other
holographic templates

00:36:15.473 --> 00:36:16.667
you might find useful.

00:36:18.309 --> 00:36:19.640
What's wrong?

00:36:19.710 --> 00:36:20.768
l'm not certain.

00:36:20.845 --> 00:36:23.109
The compression algorithms
are breaking down.

00:36:23.181 --> 00:36:25.308
l told you his program
couldn't handle that much data.

00:36:27.084 --> 00:36:29.484
What have you done to me?

00:36:40.198 --> 00:36:43.395
l'm detecting
a human life sign aboard...

00:36:43.501 --> 00:36:45.765
and a holographic signature.

00:36:45.870 --> 00:36:48.566
The vessel's weapons
are polaron-based,

00:36:48.673 --> 00:36:51.107
and they have auto-
regenerative shielding.

00:36:51.175 --> 00:36:53.939
We still have
the element of surprise.

00:36:54.078 --> 00:36:55.773
lf you don't get him
back to Voyager,

00:36:55.846 --> 00:36:57.905
his matrix will be
permanently damaged.

00:36:59.850 --> 00:37:02.045
Please do something.

00:37:02.153 --> 00:37:04.883
He won't be any use
to us if he decompiles.

00:37:18.236 --> 00:37:19.669
Someone's boarded
the Delta Flyer.

00:37:19.737 --> 00:37:20.829
They're moving away.

00:37:20.938 --> 00:37:22.405
Fire at both vessels.

00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:28.875
Now, Mr. Paris!

00:37:32.783 --> 00:37:35.047
Our shield generator
isn't going to last.

00:37:35.119 --> 00:37:38.418
lf we give them what they want,
maybe they'll leave.

00:37:40.291 --> 00:37:43.783
Prepare to jettison
their warp core.

00:37:49.166 --> 00:37:50.155
What are you doing?

00:37:50.234 --> 00:37:51.132
Arming a torpedo.

00:37:51.235 --> 00:37:52.259
lf we detonate their core,

00:37:52.370 --> 00:37:54.895
the blast wave should give us
enough time to escape.

00:37:55.006 --> 00:37:56.803
That would kill them.

00:38:02.747 --> 00:38:04.339
Captain, get down!

00:38:11.155 --> 00:38:12.986
Lieutenant, lock a tractor beam

00:38:13.057 --> 00:38:15.082
onto the core
and get it back to Voyager.

00:38:15.159 --> 00:38:16.126
Acknowledged.

00:38:29.607 --> 00:38:32.940
Nar, get this hologram off me!

00:38:42.887 --> 00:38:44.787
Guess this wasn't so useless
after all.

00:38:53.864 --> 00:38:56.662
Are you still interested
in acquiring my inventory?

00:39:06.610 --> 00:39:09.579
Computer, transfer the EMH
back into the holodeck buffer.

00:39:09.647 --> 00:39:10.978
Can you stabilize his matrix?

00:39:11.048 --> 00:39:13.983
Not until we purge
the excess subroutines.

00:39:14.051 --> 00:39:15.951
There's more than
a thousand teraquads

00:39:16.020 --> 00:39:18.648
of new data in here.

00:39:18.723 --> 00:39:19.655
How is he?

00:39:19.724 --> 00:39:21.521
We're not sure yet.

00:39:22.893 --> 00:39:25.487
Captain, if l don't survive,

00:39:25.563 --> 00:39:26.825
l need you to do
something for me.

00:39:26.897 --> 00:39:27.829
You're going to be all right.

00:39:27.898 --> 00:39:30.992
lf l'm not,
when you reach Earth,

00:39:31.102 --> 00:39:32.399
l want you to donate
my emitter

00:39:32.503 --> 00:39:33.868
to the Daystrom lnstitute.

00:39:33.938 --> 00:39:35.735
They may be able
to replicate it someday

00:39:35.806 --> 00:39:36.830
so that other holograms

00:39:36.941 --> 00:39:40.502
can know the freedom
l've enjoyed.

00:39:40.578 --> 00:39:43.046
l've had something on my
conscience for a long time.

00:39:43.114 --> 00:39:45.082
After l was first activated,

00:39:45.149 --> 00:39:47.083
l kept a record
of what l considered to be

00:39:47.151 --> 00:39:49.813
your most... questionable
command decisions.

00:39:49.887 --> 00:39:52.583
lt's in my personal database.

00:39:52.656 --> 00:39:56.353
l hope you'll delete the file
without reading it.

00:39:56.427 --> 00:39:59.885
Mr. Tuvok... l violated

00:39:59.964 --> 00:40:02.364
the most sacred trust between
a physician and his patient.

00:40:02.433 --> 00:40:04.264
l told Mr. Neelix

00:40:04.368 --> 00:40:06.802
about the cutaneous eruption
you developed on your...

00:40:09.807 --> 00:40:11.570
That was indiscreet.

00:40:11.642 --> 00:40:13.610
l hope you can forgive me.

00:40:13.711 --> 00:40:17.306
Ensign... at your recital
last month,

00:40:17.381 --> 00:40:19.645
l told Lieutenant Torres
that your saxophone playing

00:40:19.717 --> 00:40:21.742
reminded me of a wounded targ.

00:40:21.819 --> 00:40:23.844
l should've put it
more delicately.

00:40:23.921 --> 00:40:24.888
l'm sorry.

00:40:26.690 --> 00:40:28.248
Seven...

00:40:28.325 --> 00:40:29.485
You should remain still.

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:32.085
You have no idea
how difficult it's been

00:40:32.163 --> 00:40:33.824
hiding my true feelings
all these years,

00:40:33.898 --> 00:40:38.733
averting my eyes during your
regular maintenance exams.

00:40:38.836 --> 00:40:41.270
l know you could never have
the same feelings for me,

00:40:41.338 --> 00:40:42.965
but l want you
to know the truth.

00:40:43.140 --> 00:40:44.107
l love you, Seven.

00:40:47.578 --> 00:40:50.672
Your cognitive algorithms
are malfunctioning.

00:40:52.950 --> 00:40:54.178
Good-bye, my friends.

00:40:54.251 --> 00:40:57.220
Speak well of me.

00:40:57.288 --> 00:40:58.846
ls he...?

00:40:58.923 --> 00:40:59.981
No, l've got him.

00:41:06.831 --> 00:41:08.093
What happened?

00:41:08.165 --> 00:41:10.565
l deleted
the extraneous subroutines.

00:41:10.668 --> 00:41:13.296
l'm not going to decompile?

00:41:13.404 --> 00:41:16.168
You'll probably outlive us all.

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:19.539
Doc...

00:41:19.610 --> 00:41:23.341
anything else
you'd like to confess?

00:41:28.385 --> 00:41:31.946
Captain's Log, Stardate 54912.4.

00:41:32.056 --> 00:41:34.354
Lieutenant Torres has restored
our warp drive

00:41:34.425 --> 00:41:35.824
in less than a week.

00:41:35.893 --> 00:41:38.953
The Doctor's dignity, however,
might take a little longer.

00:41:39.096 --> 00:41:42.998
He hasn't left Sick Bay once
since he returned to the ship.

00:41:47.638 --> 00:41:49.799
Captain... do you need...

00:41:49.907 --> 00:41:51.272
do you need medical attention?

00:41:51.342 --> 00:41:52.536
No.

00:41:52.610 --> 00:41:54.805
You've been keeping
to yourself lately.

00:41:54.879 --> 00:41:57.313
Your friends are
worried about you.

00:42:01.685 --> 00:42:04.518
After my deathbed confession,

00:42:04.588 --> 00:42:08.684
l wasn't sure
l had any friends left.

00:42:08.759 --> 00:42:10.021
l overstepped my bounds

00:42:10.094 --> 00:42:12.824
in documenting
your command decisions.

00:42:12.897 --> 00:42:14.728
lt happened a long time ago,

00:42:14.798 --> 00:42:17.232
before l considered myself
to be a part of your crew.

00:42:17.334 --> 00:42:19.165
Oh, l'm not here
to make you grovel.

00:42:19.270 --> 00:42:20.396
l'm here to punish you

00:42:20.504 --> 00:42:21.937
for your insubordinate
behavior.

00:42:22.006 --> 00:42:24.099
l understand.

00:42:24.208 --> 00:42:25.334
You're hereby denied the use

00:42:25.409 --> 00:42:28.776
of your mobile
emitter for six days.

00:42:28.846 --> 00:42:31.076
Since you haven't left
Sick Bay for a week,

00:42:31.148 --> 00:42:34.447
we'll call it time served.

00:42:34.518 --> 00:42:36.179
l appreciate
the gesture, Captain,

00:42:36.253 --> 00:42:37.948
but l've got a lot of work
to catch up on.

00:42:38.088 --> 00:42:39.350
l'm sorry to hear that.

00:42:39.423 --> 00:42:40.685
l was hoping you
might be free

00:42:40.758 --> 00:42:43.454
for a cup of coffee
on the holodeck.

00:42:43.527 --> 00:42:46.462
l know a little sidewalk
cafe in Buenos Aires.

00:42:46.530 --> 00:42:50.489
You said you wanted
us to socialize more.

00:42:53.070 --> 00:42:55.197
l suppose Mr. Paris
can finish this.

00:42:55.306 --> 00:42:57.706
Now, when you're on the holodeck
with the Captain,

00:42:57.775 --> 00:42:59.504
there are two rules
you have to follow.

00:42:59.577 --> 00:43:00.441
l understand.

00:43:00.544 --> 00:43:01.977
First: leave your rank
at the door.

00:43:02.012 --> 00:43:03.536
Not a problem.
The second?

00:43:03.614 --> 00:43:05.377
No opera.

00:43:05.449 --> 00:43:06.575
Hmm.
